//@version=6
indicator(
     "Swing Volume Profile", shorttitle="SWINGVP", overlay=true,
     max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500,
     max_bars_back=1000
     )

// max_bars_back is REQUIRED, not decorative: every profile scan reads
// high[i]/low[i]/volume[i] with a LOOP VARIABLE, and Pine cannot infer the
// buffer depth from a dynamic index. The scan is capped by Max Bars Per Swing
// so the buffer is always sufficient.

// A horizontal volume profile built PER SWING rather than over a fixed window.
// Swings are found automatically from pivots, so the profile always describes
// the leg price is actually in — not an arbitrary last-N-bars box.
//
// Each swing gets five reference lines and a volume tag:
//   • POC       — the price row that traded the most total volume
//   • Max Buy   — the row with the most estimated BUYING
//   • Max Sell  — the row with the most estimated SELLING
//   • VAH / VAL — the edges of the value area, the band holding 70% of the
//                 swing's volume. Its EDGES are what people trade: price
//                 leaving the area is the market disagreeing with the price it
//                 spent the whole swing agreeing on.
//   • a label above each profile with the swing's total volume and buy share
//
// And ONE line that answers a question rather than describing history:
//
//   • ENTRY — the strongest volume IMBALANCE on the tradeable side of price.
//     For a buy, the row below price where buying most outweighed selling; for
//     a sell, the row above price where selling most outweighed buying. Scored
//     as (buy - sell) / busiest row, which is one number carrying both things
//     that matter: how lopsided the row was, scaled by how much volume it held.
//     A row where buyers barely won on tiny volume scores near zero, and so
//     does a huge row that was evenly matched. Neither is a level. What scores
//     high is a price where one side traded heavily and the other did not
//     answer.
//
//     IT IS A LEVEL, NOT A SIGNAL. It says where the book was heavy. It says
//     nothing about trend, direction, or whether now is the time. Below the
//     Minimum Strength input nothing is drawn at all, because a profile with no
//     strong imbalance genuinely has no level to offer and inventing one is the
//     exact failure this indicator should not have.
//
// Tuned for the 5-minute chart out of the box: Pivot Length 10 (≈50-minute
// swings), 30 rows, 3 swings. Those are inputs — raise Pivot Length on a lower
// timeframe, lower it on a higher one.
//
// HOW BUY/SELL IS ESTIMATED — the honest part:
//   Pine exposes no bid/ask, so no script can know which side was the
//   aggressor. Each bar's volume is split by where it CLOSED inside its own
//   range: a bar closing at its high counts fully as buying, at its low fully
//   as selling, in the middle 50/50.
//
//     buyShare = (close - low) / (high - low)
//
//   That is the standard approximation for a profile of this kind. It is not
//   order flow. It is right most of the time and wrong on bars that reverse
//   hard intrabar — which is exactly where you would most want it to be right.
//
//   The alternative, request.security_lower_tf(), was deliberately NOT used
//   here: on a 5-minute chart the finest intrabar resolution available on a
//   non-Premium plan is 1 minute, which is five sub-bars per candle — barely
//   better than this and far more expensive. See indicators/volume_pro for the
//   intrabar approach where it genuinely pays off.
//
// RESOLUTION: Price Rows Per Swing goes to 500. The rows are always BUILT at
//   the number you ask for, so the three marker lines get more precise with every
//   row you add — that is arrays, not drawings, and it is not rationed. What is
//   rationed is the drawing: TradingView allows 500 boxes for the whole script.
//   Rows holding no volume cost no box, the newest swing draws first, and the
//   table reports the budget in use. To buy more drawn detail: fewer swings, or
//   turn the sell|buy split off, which halves the cost per row.
//
// ACCURACY: two models, both adjustable, neither pretending to be order flow.
//   Distribution — a bar's volume is spread across the rows it spans. Even
//     gives a wick the same volume per row as the body, which is wrong in an
//     obvious way: a wick is a price the market REJECTED and traded through
//     quickly. Body-weighted is the default and puts most of the volume between
//     open and close.
//   Buy/sell split — see above. The plain close-in-range model is the default;
//     the blend also counts bar direction, which helps on trending bars and
//     hurts on choppy ones. Neither is verifiably better everywhere, so the
//     default is the well-understood one.
//
// PERFORMANCE: three tiers, because they change at three different rates.
//   A completed swing's profile is computed ONCE, when the swing closes.
//   The developing swing is recomputed once per BAR, not per tick.
//   The profile drawing — up to 492 box .set_*() calls — now also runs once per
//     bar. It used to run on every tick, redrawing a picture that was already
//     correct, and it was by far the most expensive thing this script did.
//   Only the entry level tracks live price, so only it runs per tick: one pass
//     over the rows plus two line updates.
// See references/performance-guide.md.

// ————— Constants
color TRANSPARENT_COLOR = #00000000
string THEME_DARK       = "Dark"
string THEME_LIGHT      = "Light"
int    MARKERS_PER_SWING = 5          // POC, max buy, max sell, VAH, VAL
int    MAX_ROW_BOXES     = 492        // 500 box cap, a few held in reserve
string ENTRY_BEST  = "Best Side Only"
string ENTRY_BOTH  = "Both Sides"
string ENTRY_BUY   = "Buy Side Only"
string ENTRY_SELL  = "Sell Side Only"
string DIST_BODY   = "Body-weighted"
string DIST_EVEN   = "Even"
string SPLIT_RANGE = "Close position in range"
string SPLIT_BLEND = "Range + bar direction"
// How much of a body row's volume a WICK row gets, under body-weighted
// distribution. A heuristic, not a measurement: Pine cannot say how volume
// was really spread inside a bar. What is not a heuristic is that giving a
// rejected price the same weight as a traded-through one is wrong.
float  WICK_WEIGHT  = 0.35

// ————— Inputs: Swing Detection
string SW_GROUP = "Swing Detection"
int  pivotLenInput = input.int(
     10, "Pivot Length", minval=2, maxval=200, group=SW_GROUP,
     tooltip="How many bars either side a high/low must lead to count as a swing " +
     "point. 10 suits a 5-minute chart (~50-minute swings). Raise it for fewer, " +
     "bigger swings; lower it for more, smaller ones.")
int  maxSwingsInput = input.int(
     3, "Swings To Show", minval=1, maxval=6, group=SW_GROUP)
int  maxSwingBarsInput = input.int(
     300, "Max Bars Per Swing", minval=20, maxval=900, group=SW_GROUP,
     tooltip="Safety cap. A swing longer than this is scanned only over its most " +
     "recent bars, so one runaway leg cannot stall the script.")
bool showLiveSwingInput = input.bool(
     true, "Include The Developing Swing", group=SW_GROUP,
     tooltip="Profiles the leg from the last confirmed pivot to the current bar. " +
     "It updates as the leg extends, and its shape will keep changing until the " +
     "next pivot confirms.")

// ————— Inputs: Profile
string PR_GROUP = "Profile"
int    rowsInput = input.int(
     30, "Price Rows Per Swing", minval=5, maxval=500, step=5, group=PR_GROUP,
     tooltip="Resolution of the profile. Raising it always sharpens POC / Max Buy / " +
     "Max Sell, because those are computed at full resolution whether or not every " +
     "row gets drawn. Drawing is what is limited: TradingView allows 500 boxes for " +
     "the whole script, so boxes are spent on rows that actually hold volume, newest " +
     "swing first, and the table reports the budget in use. Rows are never finer " +
     "than one tick.")
string profilePosInput = input.string(
     "Over Swing", "Profile Position",
     options=["Over Swing", "Right Of Swing"], group=PR_GROUP)
int    profileWidthInput = input.int(
     40, "Width (bars, when right of swing)", minval=5, maxval=200, group=PR_GROUP)
float  maxWidthPctInput = input.float(
     70.0, "Max Width (% of swing)", minval=10.0, maxval=100.0, step=5.0, group=PR_GROUP,
     tooltip="When drawn over the swing, the longest row spans this share of the " +
     "swing's width, so the profile never buries the candles.")
int    rowTranspInput = input.int(
     78, "Row Transparency", minval=40, maxval=97, group=PR_GROUP)
bool   showSplitInput = input.bool(
     true, "Split Each Row Into Sell | Buy", group=PR_GROUP,
     tooltip="Draws the selling share and the buying share of each row as two " +
     "segments. Off draws one bar coloured by whichever side dominated - and costs " +
     "HALF the boxes, which is the cheapest way to buy more rows.")

// ————— Inputs: Entry Levels
string EN_GROUP = "Entry Levels"
bool   showEntryInput = input.bool(
     true, "Show Entry Level", group=EN_GROUP,
     tooltip="Marks the strongest volume IMBALANCE on the tradeable side of price: " +
     "for a buy, the row below price where buying most outweighed selling; for a " +
     "sell, the row above price where selling most outweighed buying. Those are the " +
     "prices one side previously defended and the other side failed to break." +
     "\n\nIt is a level, not a signal. It says where the book was heavy, not that " +
     "the trade is good, and it says nothing at all about direction, trend or " +
     "timing. Read Strength in the table before using it: a level built on a weak " +
     "imbalance is a level that will not hold.")
string entryModeInput = input.string(
     ENTRY_BEST, "Which Side", options=[ENTRY_BEST, ENTRY_BOTH, ENTRY_BUY, ENTRY_SELL],
     group=EN_GROUP,
     tooltip="Best Side draws only the stronger of the two, which is the one the " +
     "profile actually argues for. Both Sides draws the buy level below price and " +
     "the sell level above it at the same time — useful for framing a range, " +
     "cluttered when you only want one decision.")
float  entryMinStrengthInput = input.float(
     15.0, "Minimum Strength (%)", minval=1.0, maxval=100.0, step=1.0, group=EN_GROUP,
     tooltip="How lopsided a row must be before it counts, as a percentage of the " +
     "busiest row in the swing. Below this nothing is drawn and the table says so — " +
     "a profile with no strong imbalance genuinely has no level to offer, and " +
     "inventing one would be the failure mode this input exists to prevent.")
bool   entryExtendInput = input.bool(
     true, "Extend Entry Lines Right", group=EN_GROUP)
int    entryWidthInput = input.int(
     2, "Entry Line Width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=EN_GROUP)
string entrySourceInput = input.string(
     "All shown swings", "Search For Levels In",
     options=["All shown swings", "Newest swing only"], group=EN_GROUP,
     tooltip="The strongest level available is often in an OLDER leg that price " +
     "has not come back to yet — an untested imbalance is more interesting than a " +
     "tested one, not less. Newest swing only restricts the search to the leg " +
     "price is in now, which is fresher but has less to work with early in a " +
     "swing.\n\nStrength is measured against each swing's own busiest row, so " +
     "levels from different swings stay comparable.")
bool   entryAlertInput = input.bool(
     true, "Alert When Price Reaches The Level", group=EN_GROUP,
     tooltip="Fires on bar close, once per bar. Mid-bar the touch can un-happen, " +
     "and an alert for something that never finished is worse than no alert.")

// ————— Inputs: Value Area
string VA_GROUP = "Value Area"
bool   showValueAreaInput = input.bool(
     true, "Show Value Area (VAH / VAL)", group=VA_GROUP,
     tooltip="The price band containing the given share of the swing's volume, " +
     "grown outward from the POC. It is the range the market agreed on. Its edges " +
     "matter more than its middle: price leaving the value area is the market " +
     "disagreeing, and price returning into it is the disagreement failing.")
float  valueAreaPctInput = input.float(
     70.0, "Value Area (%)", minval=30.0, maxval=95.0, step=5.0, group=VA_GROUP,
     tooltip="70% is the convention, and conventions matter here because other " +
     "traders are drawing the same line.")
color  vaColorInput = input.color(#787b86, "Value Area Color", group=VA_GROUP)

// ————— Inputs: Accuracy
string AC_GROUP = "Accuracy"
string distModeInput = input.string(
     DIST_BODY, "Volume Distribution", options=[DIST_BODY, DIST_EVEN], group=AC_GROUP,
     tooltip="How one bar's volume is spread across the price rows it spans. Even " +
     "gives a wick the same volume per row as the body, which is wrong in an " +
     "obvious way: a wick is a price the market REJECTED and traded through " +
     "quickly. Body-weighted puts most of the bar's volume between open and close " +
     "and is the better default.")
string splitModeInput = input.string(
     SPLIT_RANGE, "Buy/Sell Estimate", options=[SPLIT_RANGE, SPLIT_BLEND], group=AC_GROUP,
     tooltip="Pine exposes no bid/ask, so both of these are estimates and neither " +
     "is order flow. Close-in-range is the standard one. Range + direction also " +
     "counts whether the bar closed above or below the previous close, which helps " +
     "on trending bars and hurts on choppy ones. Neither is verifiably better " +
     "everywhere, which is why the default is left on the plain, well-understood " +
     "one rather than quietly changed under you.")
bool   showVolumeTagInput = input.bool(
     true, "Label Each Swing's Total Volume", group=AC_GROUP,
     tooltip="Prints the swing's total traded volume above its profile, with the " +
     "buy share. The developing swing is prefixed with ~ because its number is " +
     "still moving.")

// ————— Inputs: Marker Lines
string LN_GROUP = "Marker Lines"
bool   showPocInput     = input.bool(true, "POC (most total volume)", inline="poc", group=LN_GROUP)
color  pocColorInput    = input.color(#d98b1f, "", inline="poc", group=LN_GROUP)
bool   showMaxBuyInput  = input.bool(true, "Max Buy row", inline="mb", group=LN_GROUP)
color  maxBuyColorInput = input.color(#089981, "", inline="mb", group=LN_GROUP)
bool   showMaxSellInput = input.bool(true, "Max Sell row", inline="ms", group=LN_GROUP)
color  maxSellColorInput = input.color(#f23645, "", inline="ms", group=LN_GROUP)
int    lineWidthInput   = input.int(2, "Line Width", minval=1, maxval=4, group=LN_GROUP)
string lineStyleInput   = input.string(
     "Solid", "Line Style", options=["Solid", "Dashed", "Dotted"], group=LN_GROUP)
bool   extendLinesInput = input.bool(
     false, "Extend Lines Right", group=LN_GROUP,
     tooltip="Carries every marker to the right edge. Useful for the most recent " +
     "swing, cluttered when several swings are shown.")
bool   showLabelsInput  = input.bool(true, "Label The Lines", group=LN_GROUP)

// ————— Inputs: Appearance
string themeInput   = input.string(
     THEME_DARK, "Theme", options=[THEME_DARK, THEME_LIGHT], group="Appearance")
color  buyColorInput  = input.color(#089981, "Buy Color", group="Appearance")
color  sellColorInput = input.color(#f23645, "Sell Color", group="Appearance")
bool   showTableInput = input.bool(true, "Show Summary Table", group="Appearance")
string tablePosInput  = input.string(
     "Top Right", "Table Position",
     options=["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left"], group="Appearance")
bool   testModeInput  = input.bool(false, "Test Mode", group="Debug/Test")

// ————— Types
// One swing's finished profile. Holding the row arrays means a completed swing
// is scanned once and then only repositioned.
type SwingProfile
    int   leftBar
    int   rightBar
    float lo
    float step
    int   pocIdx
    int   maxBuyIdx
    int   maxSellIdx
    int   vaTopIdx
    int   vaBotIdx
    float peakRow
    float totalVol
    float buyVol
    array<float> buyRows
    array<float> sellRows

// ————— Function declarations
// @function Primary text color — the value column reads first.
getTextColor(string theme) =>
    switch theme
        THEME_LIGHT => #131722
        => #d1d4dc

// @function Secondary text color — deliberately lower contrast than the value.
getMutedColor(string theme) =>
    switch theme
        THEME_LIGHT => #4a4e58
        => #b2b5be

// @function Panel background. Low transparency on purpose: at 80+ the candles
// behind the panel win and the numbers stop being readable.
getPanelColor(string theme, int transp) =>
    color base = theme == THEME_LIGHT ? #ffffff : #131722
    color.new(base, transp)

// @function Maps a position-name string to the matching position.* constant.
tablePosFrom(string name) =>
    switch name
        "Top Left"     => position.top_left
        "Bottom Right" => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom Left"  => position.bottom_left
        => position.top_right

// @function Maps a style-name string to the matching line.style_* constant.
lineStyleFrom(string name) =>
    switch name
        "Dashed" => line.style_dashed
        "Dotted" => line.style_dotted
        => line.style_solid

// @function Compact human-readable volume ("1.24M", "345.6K").
formatVolume(float v) =>
    float av = math.abs(nz(v))
    switch
        av >= 1000000000 => str.tostring(v / 1000000000, "#.##") + "B"
        av >= 1000000    => str.tostring(v / 1000000, "#.##") + "M"
        av >= 1000       => str.tostring(v / 1000, "#.#") + "K"
        => str.tostring(nz(v), "#.#")

// @function One label/value table row. Both colors are required arguments,
// which is what stops a cell shipping without text_color — Pine defaults cell
// text to BLACK, invisible on a dark panel.
dashRow(table t, int row, string label, string value, color labelCol, color valueCol) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, row, label, text_color=labelCol, text_size=size.small,
         text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(t, 1, row, value, text_color=valueCol, text_size=size.small,
         text_halign=text.align_right)

// @function Builds the volume profile for the bars between two absolute bar
// indices. Returns na when the range is unusable, which the caller must handle.
//
// Volume is split by where each bar closed inside its own range — see the
// header. A doji contributes 50/50 rather than being dropped.
buildProfile(int leftBar, int rightBar, int rows, int scanCap) =>
    SwingProfile result = na
    int rightOff = bar_index - rightBar
    int leftOff  = math.min(bar_index - leftBar, scanCap)
    if rightOff >= 0 and leftOff > rightOff
        float hi = high[rightOff]
        float lo = low[rightOff]
        for i = rightOff to leftOff
            hi := math.max(hi, high[i])
            lo := math.min(lo, low[i])
        float span = math.max(hi - lo, syminfo.mintick)
        // Two things happen here, both of which only matter once rows go high.
        // A row finer than one tick cannot hold anything its neighbour does not,
        // so rows are reduced to the tick count the swing actually spans. And the
        // floor is one tick, NOT mintick * rows: the old floor inflated span for
        // any swing narrower than the row count, drawing a profile taller than
        // the swing it describes.
        int   useRows = math.max(5, math.min(rows, int(span / syminfo.mintick)))
        float step = span / useRows
        array<float> buys  = array.new<float>(useRows, 0.0)
        array<float> sells = array.new<float>(useRows, 0.0)
        float grandTotal = 0.0
        float grandBuy   = 0.0
        for i = rightOff to leftOff
            float barVol = nz(volume[i])
            if barVol > 0
                float barRange = high[i] - low[i]
                float rangePos = barRange > 0 ? (close[i] - low[i]) / barRange : 0.5
                float buyShare = rangePos
                if splitModeInput == SPLIT_BLEND
                    // The tick rule, at bar resolution: which way the bar closed
                    // relative to the last one. Averaged with the range position
                    // rather than replacing it, because each is wrong in a
                    // different place and neither is order flow.
                    float dirShare = close[i] > close[i + 1] ? 1.0 :
                         close[i] < close[i + 1] ? 0.0 : 0.5
                    buyShare := (rangePos + dirShare) / 2
                buyShare := math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, buyShare))
                int startIdx = int(math.floor((low[i] - lo) / step))
                int endIdx   = int(math.floor((high[i] - lo) / step))
                startIdx := math.max(0, math.min(useRows - 1, startIdx))
                endIdx   := math.max(0, math.min(useRows - 1, endIdx))
                // Body rows carry the bar's volume; wick rows carry a fraction of
                // it. A wick is a price the market REJECTED and traded through
                // quickly, so giving it the same volume per row as the body
                // overstates every extreme in the profile — which is precisely
                // where the levels people trade get drawn.
                int bodyStart = startIdx
                int bodyEnd = endIdx
                float wickWeight = 1.0
                if distModeInput == DIST_BODY
                    float bodyLo = math.min(open[i], close[i])
                    float bodyHi = math.max(open[i], close[i])
                    bodyStart := math.max(startIdx, math.min(useRows - 1,
                         int(math.floor((bodyLo - lo) / step))))
                    bodyEnd := math.min(endIdx, math.max(0,
                         int(math.floor((bodyHi - lo) / step))))
                    if bodyEnd < bodyStart
                        bodyEnd := bodyStart
                    wickWeight := WICK_WEIGHT
                int bodyCount = bodyEnd - bodyStart + 1
                int wickCount = (endIdx - startIdx + 1) - bodyCount
                // Closed form, so the weighting costs no extra pass over the rows.
                float weightSum = bodyCount + wickCount * wickWeight
                float unitVol = barVol / math.max(weightSum, 1e-10)
                for r = startIdx to endIdx
                    float w = r >= bodyStart and r <= bodyEnd ? 1.0 : wickWeight
                    float rowVol = unitVol * w
                    array.set(buys, r, array.get(buys, r) + rowVol * buyShare)
                    array.set(sells, r, array.get(sells, r) + rowVol * (1 - buyShare))
                grandTotal += barVol
                grandBuy   += barVol * buyShare
        // Three separate peaks: the row that traded most in total, the row that
        // absorbed the most buying, and the row that absorbed the most selling.
        // They are often different rows, and that difference is the signal.
        float peakTotal = 0.0
        float peakBuy   = 0.0
        float peakSell  = 0.0
        int   pocIdx = 0
        int   buyIdx = 0
        int   sellIdx = 0
        for r = 0 to useRows - 1
            float b = array.get(buys, r)
            float s = array.get(sells, r)
            if b + s > peakTotal
                peakTotal := b + s
                pocIdx := r
            if b > peakBuy
                peakBuy := b
                buyIdx := r
            if s > peakSell
                peakSell := s
                sellIdx := r
        // Value area: grow outward from the POC, always taking the heavier
        // neighbour, until the target share of the swing's volume is inside.
        // This is the standard construction, and standard matters here — other
        // traders are drawing the same two lines.
        int   vaTop = pocIdx
        int   vaBot = pocIdx
        float vaTarget = grandTotal * valueAreaPctInput / 100
        float vaVol = array.get(buys, pocIdx) + array.get(sells, pocIdx)
        // Bounded by the row count: each pass moves at least one edge, so it can
        // never run longer than there are rows, whatever the volume looks like.
        for _step = 1 to useRows
            if vaVol >= vaTarget or (vaBot <= 0 and vaTop >= useRows - 1)
                break
            float above = vaTop < useRows - 1 ?
                 array.get(buys, vaTop + 1) + array.get(sells, vaTop + 1) : -1.0
            float below = vaBot > 0 ?
                 array.get(buys, vaBot - 1) + array.get(sells, vaBot - 1) : -1.0
            if above >= below
                vaTop += 1
                vaVol += above
            else
                vaBot -= 1
                vaVol += below
        if peakTotal > 0
            result := SwingProfile.new(
                 leftBar = math.max(leftBar, bar_index - leftOff), rightBar = rightBar,
                 lo = lo, step = step, pocIdx = pocIdx, maxBuyIdx = buyIdx,
                 maxSellIdx = sellIdx, vaTopIdx = vaTop, vaBotIdx = vaBot,
                 peakRow = peakTotal, totalVol = grandTotal,
                 buyVol = grandBuy, buyRows = buys, sellRows = sells)
    result

// @function Price at the centre of a profile row.
rowPrice(SwingProfile p, int idx) =>
    p.lo + (idx + 0.5) * p.step

// @function The strongest volume imbalance on each side of a price.
//
// Returns [buyIdx, buyStrength, sellIdx, sellStrength]; an index of -1 means
// that side has nothing worth drawing.
//
// The score is (buy - sell) / peakRow, which is one number carrying both things
// that matter: how lopsided the row was, scaled by how much volume it held.
// A row where buyers barely won on tiny volume scores near zero, and so does a
// huge row that was evenly matched. Neither is a level. What scores high is a
// price where one side traded heavily and the other side did not answer.
//
// Priced off the row CENTRES, and evaluated against live price, so this is the
// only part of the drawing that has to run on every tick.
bestEntry(SwingProfile p, float price, float minStrength) =>
    int rows = array.size(p.buyRows)
    int   buyIdx = -1
    int   sellIdx = -1
    float buyBest = minStrength
    float sellBest = minStrength
    if p.peakRow > 0 and rows > 0
        for r = 0 to rows - 1
            float rowMid = p.lo + (r + 0.5) * p.step
            float imbalance = (array.get(p.buyRows, r) - array.get(p.sellRows, r)) / p.peakRow
            if rowMid < price and imbalance > buyBest
                buyBest := imbalance
                buyIdx := r
            if rowMid > price and -imbalance > sellBest
                sellBest := -imbalance
                sellIdx := r
    [buyIdx, buyIdx >= 0 ? buyBest : 0.0, sellIdx, sellIdx >= 0 ? sellBest : 0.0]

// @function Grows a box pool, parking new boxes invisibly.
ensureBoxPool(array<box> pool, int needed) =>
    while array.size(pool) < needed
        array.push(pool, box.new(
             bar_index, close, bar_index, close, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             bgcolor=TRANSPARENT_COLOR, border_color=TRANSPARENT_COLOR))

// @function Grows a line pool.
ensureLinePool(array<line> pool, int needed) =>
    while array.size(pool) < needed
        array.push(pool, line.new(
             bar_index, close, bar_index, close, xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             color=TRANSPARENT_COLOR))

// @function Grows a label pool.
ensureLabelPool(array<label> pool, int needed) =>
    while array.size(pool) < needed
        array.push(pool, label.new(
             bar_index, close, "", xloc=xloc.bar_index,
             style=label.style_label_left, color=TRANSPARENT_COLOR))

// @function Hides pool boxes from `from` onward so a shrinking draw leaves
// nothing stale behind.
hideBoxesFrom(array<box> pool, int from) =>
    if array.size(pool) > from
        for i = from to array.size(pool) - 1
            box.set_bgcolor(array.get(pool, i), TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
            box.set_border_color(array.get(pool, i), TRANSPARENT_COLOR)

// @function Hides pool lines from `from` onward.
hideLinesFrom(array<line> pool, int from) =>
    if array.size(pool) > from
        for i = from to array.size(pool) - 1
            line.set_color(array.get(pool, i), TRANSPARENT_COLOR)

// @function Hides pool labels from `from` onward.
hideLabelsFrom(array<label> pool, int from) =>
    if array.size(pool) > from
        for i = from to array.size(pool) - 1
            label.set_text(array.get(pool, i), "")

// ————— Calculations: budget
// Boxes are capped at 500 for the whole script, and the profile rows are the
// only consumer — the marker lines and their tags come out of the separate line
// and label pools.
//
// Rows are BUILT at the resolution you ask for, always. That is the part that
// decides how precise POC / Max Buy / Max Sell are, and it costs arrays, not
// boxes. Only the drawing is rationed, and it is rationed by spending boxes on
// rows that actually hold volume — at high resolution most rows in a swing are
// empty, and an empty row now costs nothing at all. Newest swing draws first, so
// if the budget does run out it is the oldest swing that thins, not the live one.
int boxesPerRow    = showSplitInput ? 2 : 1
int profileRows    = rowsInput

color textColor  = getTextColor(themeInput)
color mutedColor = getMutedColor(themeInput)
string markerStyle = lineStyleFrom(lineStyleInput)

// ————— Calculations: swing detection
float pivotHigh = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLenInput, pivotLenInput)
float pivotLow  = ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLenInput, pivotLenInput)
bool  newPivot  = not na(pivotHigh) or not na(pivotLow)

// Absolute bar index of every confirmed pivot, newest last. `var` matters: a
// pivot can appear mid-bar and vanish before the bar closes, and only var's
// rollback keeps a phantom from being recorded permanently.
var array<int> pivotBars = array.new<int>()
var array<SwingProfile> swings = array.new<SwingProfile>()

// Bumped by every change to the set of profiles. The drawing compares against
// it rather than against the swing count, because a push plus a drop on the
// same tick leaves the count identical and the picture wrong.
var int profileGen = 0

if newPivot
    int pivotBar = bar_index - pivotLenInput
    // Build the profile for the leg that just closed, then keep only the most
    // recent ones. A completed swing never changes, so this runs once per swing.
    if array.size(pivotBars) > 0
        int prevBar = array.get(pivotBars, array.size(pivotBars) - 1)
        SwingProfile finished = buildProfile(prevBar, pivotBar, profileRows, maxSwingBarsInput)
        if not na(finished)
            array.push(swings, finished)
            profileGen += 1
            while array.size(swings) > maxSwingsInput
                array.shift(swings)
                profileGen += 1
    array.push(pivotBars, pivotBar)
    while array.size(pivotBars) > maxSwingsInput + 2
        array.shift(pivotBars)

// The developing leg: last confirmed pivot to the current bar. Memoised on
// bar_index so it recomputes once per bar rather than on every realtime tick —
// its shape cannot meaningfully change within one 5-minute candle.
var SwingProfile liveSwing = na
var int liveCachedBar = na
if showLiveSwingInput and array.size(pivotBars) > 0
    bool needsRebuild = na(liveCachedBar) or liveCachedBar != bar_index
    if needsRebuild
        liveCachedBar := bar_index
        int lastPivot = array.get(pivotBars, array.size(pivotBars) - 1)
        liveSwing := buildProfile(lastPivot, bar_index, profileRows, maxSwingBarsInput)
        profileGen += 1

// ————— Visuals: pools
var array<box>   rowBoxes    = array.new<box>()
var int          boxesUsed   = 0
var array<line>  markerLines = array.new<line>()
var array<label> markerTags  = array.new<label>()

// The entry level is the one drawing that depends on live price, so it lives in
// its own pool and updates on every tick while everything else does not.
var array<line>  entryLines = array.new<line>()
var array<label> entryTags  = array.new<label>()
var array<label> volumeTags = array.new<label>()

// Live state, published so the table and the alerts read the same numbers the
// chart is showing rather than recomputing them and drifting.
var float entryBuyPrice   = na
var float entrySellPrice  = na
var float entryBuyPower   = 0.0
var float entrySellPower  = 0.0


// @function Draws one swing's rows into the box pool starting at `cursor`,
// stopping before box index `limit`, and returns how many boxes it used.
//
// A row holding no volume consumes NO box. That is what makes a high row count
// affordable: the rows a profile actually needs are the ones price traded in.
drawRows(SwingProfile p, array<box> pool, int cursor, int limit, int rightEdge, int leftEdge) =>
    int used = 0
    int rows = array.size(p.buyRows)
    int cost = showSplitInput ? 2 : 1
    int fullWidth = math.max(1, rightEdge - leftEdge)
    for r = 0 to rows - 1
        // Out of budget: every remaining row would be skipped anyway, and at 500
        // rows a swing the wasted iterations are not free.
        if cursor + used + cost > limit
            break
        float b = array.get(p.buyRows, r)
        float s = array.get(p.sellRows, r)
        float t = b + s
        float yBot = p.lo + r * p.step
        if t > 0 and p.peakRow > 0
            int rowWidth = math.max(1, int(fullWidth * (t / p.peakRow)))
            if showSplitInput
                // Sell segment first, then buy — so the split reads left to
                // right in the same order every time.
                int sellWidth = math.max(0, int(rowWidth * (t > 0 ? s / t : 0.0)))
                box sellBox = array.get(pool, cursor + used)
                box.set_lefttop(sellBox, leftEdge, yBot + p.step)
                box.set_rightbottom(sellBox, leftEdge + sellWidth, yBot)
                box.set_bgcolor(sellBox, color.new(sellColorInput, rowTranspInput))
                box.set_border_color(sellBox, TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
                used += 1
                box buyBox = array.get(pool, cursor + used)
                box.set_lefttop(buyBox, leftEdge + sellWidth, yBot + p.step)
                box.set_rightbottom(buyBox, leftEdge + rowWidth, yBot)
                box.set_bgcolor(buyBox, color.new(buyColorInput, rowTranspInput))
                box.set_border_color(buyBox, TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
                used += 1
            else
                box bx = array.get(pool, cursor + used)
                box.set_lefttop(bx, leftEdge, yBot + p.step)
                box.set_rightbottom(bx, leftEdge + rowWidth, yBot)
                box.set_bgcolor(bx, color.new(b >= s ? buyColorInput : sellColorInput, rowTranspInput))
                box.set_border_color(bx, TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
                used += 1
    used

// @function Prints a swing's total traded volume above its profile.
// `settled` is false for the leg still forming, whose number is still moving.
drawVolumeTag(SwingProfile p, label lb, int x, float topPrice, bool settled) =>
    float buyPct = p.totalVol > 0 ? p.buyVol / p.totalVol * 100 : na
    string prefix = settled ? "" : "~"
    label.set_xy(lb, x, topPrice)
    label.set_text(lb, prefix + formatVolume(p.totalVol) +
         (na(buyPct) ? "" : "  " + str.tostring(buyPct, "#") + "% buy"))
    label.set_textcolor(lb, na(buyPct) or buyPct >= 50 ? buyColorInput : sellColorInput)
    label.set_size(lb, size.small)
    label.set_style(lb, label.style_label_down)
    label.set_color(lb, TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
    label.set_tooltip(lb, (settled ? "Completed swing" : "Developing swing — still changing") +
         "\nTotal volume: " + formatVolume(p.totalVol) +
         "\nBuying: " + formatVolume(p.buyVol) +
         "\nSelling: " + formatVolume(p.totalVol - p.buyVol) +
         "\nBars: " + str.tostring(p.rightBar - p.leftBar + 1) +
         "\nRows: " + str.tostring(array.size(p.buyRows)))

// @function Draws one marker line (and optional label), returning 1 if it was
// used so the caller can advance its cursor.
drawMarker(bool enabled, float price, string tag, color col, array<line> linePool,
     array<label> labelPool, int lineCursor, int labelCursor, int leftEdge, int rightEdge) =>
    int used = 0
    if enabled and not na(price)
        line ln = array.get(linePool, lineCursor)
        line.set_xy1(ln, leftEdge, price)
        line.set_xy2(ln, rightEdge, price)
        line.set_color(ln, col)
        line.set_width(ln, lineWidthInput)
        line.set_style(ln, markerStyle)
        line.set_extend(ln, extendLinesInput ? extend.right : extend.none)
        label lb = array.get(labelPool, labelCursor)
        if showLabelsInput
            label.set_xy(lb, rightEdge, price)
            label.set_text(lb, tag + "  " + str.tostring(price, format.mintick))
            label.set_textcolor(lb, col)
            label.set_size(lb, size.small)
        else
            label.set_text(lb, "")
        used := 1
    used

// @function Draws one entry level and its label.
drawEntry(line ln, label lb, float price, float power, bool isBuy, int leftBar) =>
    color col = isBuy ? buyColorInput : sellColorInput
    line.set_xy1(ln, leftBar, price)
    line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, price)
    line.set_color(ln, col)
    line.set_width(ln, entryWidthInput)
    line.set_style(ln, line.style_solid)
    line.set_extend(ln, entryExtendInput ? extend.right : extend.none)
    label.set_xy(lb, bar_index, price)
    label.set_text(lb, (isBuy ? "BUY " : "SELL ") + str.tostring(price, format.mintick) +
         "  " + str.tostring(power * 100, "#") + "%")
    label.set_textcolor(lb, col)
    label.set_size(lb, size.small)
    label.set_style(lb, label.style_label_left)
    label.set_color(lb, TRANSPARENT_COLOR)
    label.set_tooltip(lb,
         (isBuy ? "Strongest BUY imbalance below price" : "Strongest SELL imbalance above price") +
         "\nStrength: " + str.tostring(power * 100, "#.#") + "% of the busiest row" +
         "\nDistance: " + str.tostring(math.abs(close - price), format.mintick) +
         "\n\nThis is a level, not a signal. It marks where one side traded " +
         "heavily and the other did not answer — it says nothing about trend, " +
         "direction or timing.")


// ————— Visuals: the profile, redrawn once per bar
//
// Nothing in this block depends on live price, and the profiles themselves only
// change when a bar closes or a pivot confirms. Running it on every tick meant
// up to 492 box .set_*() calls to redraw a picture that was already correct —
// the single most expensive thing this script did, repeated for no reason. The
// entry level, which genuinely does track price, is drawn separately below.
//
// The generation counter is part of the trigger, not just the bar: a pivot can
// confirm mid-bar, and a new swing must not wait for the next candle to appear.
var int drawnBar = na
var int drawnGen = -1
int swingCount = array.size(swings)
int liveCount  = na(liveSwing) ? 0 : 1
int totalSwings = swingCount + liveCount
bool profileNeedsRedraw = na(drawnBar) or drawnBar != bar_index or drawnGen != profileGen

if barstate.islast and profileNeedsRedraw
    drawnBar := bar_index
    drawnGen := profileGen
    // Ask for what the swings would use, capped by what TradingView allows.
    int poolSize = math.min(
         MAX_ROW_BOXES, math.max(1, totalSwings * profileRows * boxesPerRow))
    ensureBoxPool(rowBoxes, poolSize)
    ensureLinePool(markerLines, math.max(1, totalSwings * MARKERS_PER_SWING))
    ensureLabelPool(markerTags, math.max(1, totalSwings * MARKERS_PER_SWING))
    ensureLabelPool(volumeTags, math.max(1, totalSwings))

    int boxCursor = 0
    int lineCursor = 0
    int tagCursor = 0
    // The guard is not cosmetic: Pine counts DOWN when a for-loop's end value is
    // below its start, so `0 to totalSwings - 1` with no swings yet would run
    // with i = 0 and i = -1 and index an empty array.
    if totalSwings > 0
        for k = 0 to totalSwings - 1
            // Newest first. If the box budget runs out it must be the oldest
            // swing that loses rows, never the leg price is trading in now.
            int i = totalSwings - 1 - k
            SwingProfile p = i < swingCount ? array.get(swings, i) : liveSwing
            if not na(p)
                int leftEdge = p.leftBar
                int rightEdge = p.rightBar
                if profilePosInput == "Right Of Swing"
                    leftEdge := p.rightBar
                    rightEdge := p.rightBar + profileWidthInput
                else
                    // Cap how far the longest row reaches so the profile never
                    // buries the candles it is describing.
                    int swingWidth = math.max(1, p.rightBar - p.leftBar)
                    rightEdge := p.leftBar + math.max(1, int(swingWidth * maxWidthPctInput / 100))
                boxCursor += drawRows(p, rowBoxes, boxCursor, poolSize, rightEdge, leftEdge)
                int markerRight = profilePosInput == "Right Of Swing" ?
                     p.rightBar + profileWidthInput : p.rightBar
                lineCursor += drawMarker(
                     showPocInput, rowPrice(p, p.pocIdx), "POC", pocColorInput,
                     markerLines, markerTags, lineCursor, lineCursor, p.leftBar, markerRight)
                lineCursor += drawMarker(
                     showMaxBuyInput, rowPrice(p, p.maxBuyIdx), "MAX BUY", maxBuyColorInput,
                     markerLines, markerTags, lineCursor, lineCursor, p.leftBar, markerRight)
                lineCursor += drawMarker(
                     showMaxSellInput, rowPrice(p, p.maxSellIdx), "MAX SELL", maxSellColorInput,
                     markerLines, markerTags, lineCursor, lineCursor, p.leftBar, markerRight)
                // The value area's EDGES are what people trade — price leaving
                // the area is the market disagreeing with the price it spent
                // most of the swing agreeing on.
                lineCursor += drawMarker(
                     showValueAreaInput, rowPrice(p, p.vaTopIdx), "VAH", vaColorInput,
                     markerLines, markerTags, lineCursor, lineCursor, p.leftBar, markerRight)
                lineCursor += drawMarker(
                     showValueAreaInput, rowPrice(p, p.vaBotIdx), "VAL", vaColorInput,
                     markerLines, markerTags, lineCursor, lineCursor, p.leftBar, markerRight)
                if showVolumeTagInput
                    float profileTop = p.lo + array.size(p.buyRows) * p.step
                    drawVolumeTag(p, array.get(volumeTags, tagCursor),
                         int((leftEdge + rightEdge) / 2), profileTop, i < swingCount)
                    tagCursor += 1
    boxesUsed := boxCursor
    hideBoxesFrom(rowBoxes, boxCursor)
    hideLinesFrom(markerLines, lineCursor)
    hideLabelsFrom(markerTags, lineCursor)
    hideLabelsFrom(volumeTags, tagCursor)

// ————— Visuals: the entry level, every tick
//
// This is the only drawing that depends on live price, so it is the only one
// that has to be recomputed while a bar is open. One pass over the rows.
if barstate.islast
    ensureLinePool(entryLines, 2)
    ensureLabelPool(entryTags, 2)
    entryBuyPrice  := na
    entrySellPrice := na
    entryBuyPower  := 0.0
    entrySellPower := 0.0
    int entryCursor = 0

    if showEntryInput and totalSwings > 0
        float bestBuyPrice  = na
        float bestSellPrice = na
        float bestBuyPower  = 0.0
        float bestSellPower = 0.0
        int   bestBuyLeft   = bar_index
        int   bestSellLeft  = bar_index
        // Searching every drawn swing, not just the newest: the strongest level
        // available is often in an older leg price has not returned to yet, and
        // an untested imbalance is more interesting than a tested one.
        int searchFrom = entrySourceInput == "Newest swing only" ? totalSwings - 1 : 0
        for i = searchFrom to totalSwings - 1
            SwingProfile p = i < swingCount ? array.get(swings, i) : liveSwing
            if not na(p)
                [bIdx, bPow, sIdx, sPow] = bestEntry(p, close, entryMinStrengthInput / 100)
                if bIdx >= 0 and bPow > bestBuyPower
                    bestBuyPower := bPow
                    bestBuyPrice := rowPrice(p, bIdx)
                    bestBuyLeft  := p.leftBar
                if sIdx >= 0 and sPow > bestSellPower
                    bestSellPower := sPow
                    bestSellPrice := rowPrice(p, sIdx)
                    bestSellLeft  := p.leftBar

        bool haveBuy  = not na(bestBuyPrice)
        bool haveSell = not na(bestSellPrice)
        // Best Side draws only the level the profile actually argues for.
        bool drawBuy = switch entryModeInput
            ENTRY_BUY  => haveBuy
            ENTRY_SELL => false
            ENTRY_BOTH => haveBuy
            => haveBuy and bestBuyPower >= bestSellPower
        bool drawSell = switch entryModeInput
            ENTRY_BUY  => false
            ENTRY_SELL => haveSell
            ENTRY_BOTH => haveSell
            => haveSell and bestSellPower > bestBuyPower
        // Published only when DRAWN. Publishing a level that is not on the chart
        // would let the alert fire for something the user cannot see, which is
        // the kind of inconsistency that makes an indicator untrustworthy.
        if drawBuy
            entryBuyPrice := bestBuyPrice
            entryBuyPower := bestBuyPower
            drawEntry(array.get(entryLines, entryCursor), array.get(entryTags, entryCursor),
                 bestBuyPrice, bestBuyPower, true, bestBuyLeft)
            entryCursor += 1
        if drawSell
            entrySellPrice := bestSellPrice
            entrySellPower := bestSellPower
            drawEntry(array.get(entryLines, entryCursor), array.get(entryTags, entryCursor),
                 bestSellPrice, bestSellPower, false, bestSellLeft)
            entryCursor += 1
    hideLinesFrom(entryLines, entryCursor)
    hideLabelsFrom(entryTags, entryCursor)

// ————— Visuals: summary table
var table dash = table.new(
     tablePosFrom(tablePosInput), 2, 12,
     bgcolor=getPanelColor(themeInput, 15), border_width=1,
     border_color=getPanelColor(themeInput, 100),
     frame_color=color.new(mutedColor, 70), frame_width=1)

if showTableInput and barstate.islast
    SwingProfile shown = na(liveSwing) ?
         (swingCount > 0 ? array.get(swings, swingCount - 1) : na) : liveSwing
    bool haveSwing = not na(shown)
    float buyPct = haveSwing and shown.totalVol > 0 ? shown.buyVol / shown.totalVol * 100 : na

    // The entry row first: it is the only line on the chart that answers a
    // question rather than describing history, so burying it under six
    // reference prices would be the wrong order.
    bool buyIsBest = not na(entryBuyPrice) and
         (na(entrySellPrice) or entryBuyPower >= entrySellPower)
    float shownEntry = buyIsBest ? entryBuyPrice : entrySellPrice
    float shownPower = buyIsBest ? entryBuyPower : entrySellPower
    color entryColor = buyIsBest ? buyColorInput : sellColorInput
    string entryText = na(shownEntry) ? "none" :
         (buyIsBest ? "BUY " : "SELL ") + str.tostring(shownEntry, format.mintick)

    // Two different numbers, and conflating them is what would mislead you:
    // rows is the resolution the profile was BUILT at, boxes is how much of the
    // drawing budget that resolution is currently spending.
    int shownRows = haveSwing ? array.size(shown.buyRows) : 0
    string rowNote = not haveSwing ? "--" :
         shownRows < rowsInput ?
         str.tostring(shownRows) + " / " + str.tostring(rowsInput) + " (tick limit)" :
         str.tostring(shownRows)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "SWING PROFILE", text_color=textColor, text_size=size.normal,
         text_halign=text.align_center)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, "", text_color=textColor)
    table.merge_cells(dash, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    dashRow(dash, 1, "Entry level", entryText, mutedColor,
         na(shownEntry) ? mutedColor : entryColor)
    dashRow(dash, 2, "Strength", na(shownEntry) ? "--" :
         str.tostring(shownPower * 100, "#.#") + "%", mutedColor,
         na(shownEntry) ? mutedColor : entryColor)
    dashRow(dash, 3, "Distance", na(shownEntry) ? "--" :
         str.tostring(math.abs(close - shownEntry), format.mintick) + "  (" +
         str.tostring(math.abs(close - shownEntry) / close * 100, "#.##") + "%)",
         mutedColor, textColor)

    dashRow(dash, 4, "Swing volume", haveSwing ? formatVolume(shown.totalVol) : "--",
         mutedColor, textColor)
    dashRow(dash, 5, "Buy share", na(buyPct) ? "--" : str.tostring(buyPct, "#.#") + "%",
         mutedColor, nz(buyPct, 50) >= 50 ? buyColorInput : sellColorInput)
    dashRow(dash, 6, "POC", haveSwing ? str.tostring(rowPrice(shown, shown.pocIdx), format.mintick) : "--",
         mutedColor, pocColorInput)
    dashRow(dash, 7, "Value area", haveSwing ?
         str.tostring(rowPrice(shown, shown.vaBotIdx), format.mintick) + " - " +
         str.tostring(rowPrice(shown, shown.vaTopIdx), format.mintick) : "--",
         mutedColor, vaColorInput)
    dashRow(dash, 8, "Max buy", haveSwing ?
         str.tostring(rowPrice(shown, shown.maxBuyIdx), format.mintick) : "--",
         mutedColor, maxBuyColorInput)
    dashRow(dash, 9, "Max sell", haveSwing ?
         str.tostring(rowPrice(shown, shown.maxSellIdx), format.mintick) : "--",
         mutedColor, maxSellColorInput)
    dashRow(dash, 10, "Rows / swing", rowNote, mutedColor,
         shownRows < rowsInput ? pocColorInput : textColor)
    dashRow(dash, 11, "Boxes used",
         str.tostring(boxesUsed) + " / " + str.tostring(MAX_ROW_BOXES), mutedColor,
         boxesUsed >= MAX_ROW_BOXES ? pocColorInput : textColor)

// ————— Alerts
alertcondition(newPivot, "New swing confirmed", "A new swing pivot has been confirmed.")

// Gated on bar close, deliberately. Mid-bar a touch can un-happen, and an alert
// for something that never finished is worse than no alert at all.
if entryAlertInput and barstate.islast and barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(entryBuyPrice) and low <= entryBuyPrice and high >= entryBuyPrice
        alert("Price reached the BUY level at " +
             str.tostring(entryBuyPrice, format.mintick) + " (strength " +
             str.tostring(entryBuyPower * 100, "#") + "%) on " + syminfo.ticker,
             alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    if not na(entrySellPrice) and low <= entrySellPrice and high >= entrySellPrice
        alert("Price reached the SELL level at " +
             str.tostring(entrySellPrice, format.mintick) + " (strength " +
             str.tostring(entrySellPower * 100, "#") + "%) on " + syminfo.ticker,
             alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ————— Debug / Test block (keep testModeInput false when handing off)
int TEST_COUNT = 8      // keep in sync with the assertFailed() calls below
var int passCount = 0
var int failCount = 0

// @function Draws a failure marker and RETURNS 1 on failure, 0 on pass. Pine
// forbids a function from modifying a global (CE10088), so the counting happens
// at the call site.
assertFailed(bool condition, string description) =>
    if not condition
        label.new(bar_index, high, "FAIL: " + description, color=sellColorInput,
             textcolor=color.white, style=label.style_label_down, size=size.small)
    condition ? 0 : 1

if testModeInput
    int fails = 0
    // 1. The stored swings must never exceed the configured cap.
    fails += assertFailed(array.size(swings) <= maxSwingsInput, "swing list exceeded its cap")
    // 2. Every marker index must be inside the row range.
    fails += assertFailed(
         na(liveSwing) or (liveSwing.pocIdx >= 0 and
         liveSwing.pocIdx < array.size(liveSwing.buyRows) and
         liveSwing.maxBuyIdx >= 0 and
         liveSwing.maxBuyIdx < array.size(liveSwing.buyRows) and
         liveSwing.maxSellIdx >= 0 and
         liveSwing.maxSellIdx < array.size(liveSwing.buyRows)),
         "marker row index out of range")
    // 3. Buying can never exceed the volume the swing actually traded.
    fails += assertFailed(
         na(liveSwing) or liveSwing.buyVol <= liveSwing.totalVol + 1,
         "buy volume exceeds total volume")
    // 4. A profile row must have positive height, and never be finer than a tick.
    fails += assertFailed(
         na(liveSwing) or liveSwing.step >= syminfo.mintick * 0.999,
         "profile row is thinner than one tick")
    // 5. The drawing must never exceed the box budget it was given.
    fails += assertFailed(boxesUsed <= MAX_ROW_BOXES, "row boxes exceeded the budget")
    // 6. The value area must contain the POC and stay inside the row range.
    fails += assertFailed(
         na(liveSwing) or (liveSwing.vaBotIdx <= liveSwing.pocIdx and
         liveSwing.vaTopIdx >= liveSwing.pocIdx and liveSwing.vaBotIdx >= 0 and
         liveSwing.vaTopIdx < array.size(liveSwing.buyRows)),
         "value area does not bracket the POC")
    // 7. A buy level must sit BELOW price and a sell level ABOVE it. Getting
    //    this backwards would be the worst failure available to this script:
    //    a level that looks authoritative and is on the wrong side.
    fails += assertFailed(
         (na(entryBuyPrice) or entryBuyPrice < close) and
         (na(entrySellPrice) or entrySellPrice > close),
         "entry level is on the wrong side of price")
    // 8. A drawn level must clear the strength floor it claims to respect.
    fails += assertFailed(
         (na(entryBuyPrice) or entryBuyPower >= entryMinStrengthInput / 100) and
         (na(entrySellPrice) or entrySellPower >= entryMinStrengthInput / 100),
         "entry level is below the minimum strength")
    failCount += fails
    passCount += TEST_COUNT - fails

var table testTable = table.new(
     position.bottom_left, 2, 2, border_width=1,
     bgcolor=getPanelColor(themeInput, 15),
     frame_color=color.new(mutedColor, 70), frame_width=1)
if testModeInput and barstate.islast
    dashRow(testTable, 0, "Passed", str.tostring(passCount), mutedColor, buyColorInput)
    dashRow(testTable, 1, "Failed", str.tostring(failCount), mutedColor,
         failCount > 0 ? sellColorInput : buyColorInput)
